        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Forsythia koreana, commonly called gaenari (Hangul: 개나리) or Korean goldenbell tree, is a species in the olive family, Oleaceae. It grows to about {{convert|3|m|ft|abbr=on}}. The leaves are oval in shape, have teeth, and are {{convert|3-12|cm|in|abbr=on}} long. The front of the leaf is dark green and the back is dark blue, but both sides are hairless."
          }
        ]
      }
